Video Game Enemy Spawner

-> You are building an RPG game. You have a complex Enemy class that takes a
   long time to instantiate because it has to load heavy 3D mesh data, textures,
   and AI behavior trees from the disk. When the player enters a dungeon, you
   need to spawn 50 Goblins. Creating each one from scratch via the new keyword
   creates a massive performance lag.

 -> Task: Implement a cloning mechanism to duplicate an existing object instead
          of creating it from scratch.
 1. Create a base Enemy interface with a clone() method.
 2. Create a Goblin class that implements this interface.
 3. Instantiate one "Master Goblin" at the start of the game. When the dungeon loads,
    use the clone() method to create the 50 enemies instantly.
 4. Bonus challenge: Ensure your clone is a "deep copy" so that modifying the health
    of one cloned goblin doesn't accidentally reduce the health of all the others!